{\n  \"_note\": \"Radar drop file (batch_2026-07-18, evening rescan). One entry: Fed Chair Kevin Warsh July 14, 2026 House Financial Services testimony — crypto/fintech Q&A statements on no-bailout stance for crypto/stablecoins, GENIUS Act rulemaking urgency, and nonbank fintech payment-system access. Captured in evening rescan; timing gap from batch_2026-07-14 (ran 09:00Z, before 10:00 ET hearing). Verified via Tier 1 primary (federalreserve.gov) + 2 Tier 3 secondaries (Law360, CCN/Yahoo Finance). Merged into items.json by merge_incoming.py; idempotent on id. Infrastructure note: merge.yml still not installed in this repo — this drop file will not auto-merge until TG installs merge.yml or runs merge_incoming.py manually (same issue as incoming/2026-07-17.json).\",\n  \"entries\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"2026-07-18-warsh-house-testimony-crypto-no-bailout\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-07-14\",\n      \"published\": \"2026-07-18T21:00:00Z\",\n      \"issuing_body\": \"Federal Reserve Board\",\n      \"title\": \"Fed Chair Warsh testifies to House Financial Services: no Federal Reserve bailout for crypto or stablecoins; Fed 'racing' to meet GENIUS Act stablecoin rulemaking deadline; nonbank fintech payment access pressed\",\n      \"facts\": \"Federal Reserve Chairman Kevin Warsh testified before the House Committee on Financial Services on July 14, 2026, as part of the Semiannual Monetary Policy Report (2128 Rayburn House Office Building, 10:00 AM). The official prepared statement focused on price stability, monetary policy, and internal Fed task forces. During the Q&A, Warsh made three statements directly relevant to crypto, stablecoin, and fintech operators: (1) No Federal Reserve bailout for crypto or stablecoins: Pressed by Rep. Brad Sherman on whether the Fed would provide the kind of support it gave money market funds in 2008, Warsh stated 'We do not want to be in the bailout business, full stop.' He added that the Fed would 'do everything we can to mitigate... extraordinary risks' but would not bail out crypto. He did not fully rule out marginal systemic-spillover mitigation. (2) GENIUS Act rulemaking urgency: Warsh told lawmakers the Fed is 'racing' to finalize its portion of the GENIUS Act stablecoin implementing rules ahead of the July 18, 2026 one-year statutory deadline. The deadline has since been confirmed missed (the Federal Register contains no in-scope publication; July 18 is a Saturday; earliest possible publication is Monday July 20). (3) Nonbank fintech payment-system access: Rep. Sherman separately pressed on Kraken's pending bank application and nonbank crypto firms seeking direct access to the payment system; Warsh invoked systemic-risk considerations without making a specific commitment. Background: Warsh is the most crypto-sympathetic Fed Chair on record, having previously disclosed venture stakes in Bitcoin payments, a crypto index manager, Bitwise, and a stablecoin venture — all divested under Fed ethics rules prior to confirmation in May 2026. A 2026 New York Fed staff report cited in contemporaneous coverage found stablecoin activity can transmit liquidity stress to banks and complicate monetary policy. This is Warsh's first congressional testimony since his confirmation. Secondary coverage: Law360, July 14, 2026 ('Fed Racing To Hit Genius Act Rules Deadline, Warsh Says'); CCN via Yahoo Finance, July 15, 2026 ('Fed Chair Kevin Warsh Says Crypto and Stablecoins Are On Their Own in a Crisis').\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/testimony/warsh20260714a.htm\",\n      \"source_label\": \"Federal Reserve Board — Semiannual Monetary Policy Report Testimony, Chairman Kevin Warsh, House Committee on Financial Services, July 14, 2026\",\n      \"source_type\": \"primary_source\",\n      \"primary_source_status\": \"retrieved\",\n      \"relevant_to\": \"stablecoin issuers, crypto banks, nonbank payment providers, fintech firms seeking Fed master accounts, crypto exchanges with pending bank applications\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"stablecoin\",\n        \"digital-assets\",\n        \"fintech\",\n        \"crypto-banking\",\n        \"fed\",\n        \"testimony\",\n        \"genius-act\",\n        \"no-bailout\",\n        \"master-account\",\n        \"payment-system-access\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}